# Managed by home/srvs/nix-docs.nix; edits here are overwritten.
#
# ONE rule, on purpose.
#
# Everything else under docs/ is prose somebody wrote by hand — a runbook, a
# roadmap, an impact analysis — and for prose the right answer to "both machines
# edited this" is still a loud conflict that stops and asks a human. Union would
# silently duplicate paragraphs; last-writer-wins would silently delete one
# side's work. nix-docs.nix argues that at length and it has not changed.
#
# board.md is different in kind. It is a STORE, not a document: an unattended
# writer on each machine (board-watch's agents), a GUI on each machine, and a
# five-minute window between them, so two-sided edits are routine rather than
# exceptional. Wedging the whole docs sync until someone notices — which is what
# an unresolved conflict does here — is the one outcome it must never produce.
#
# The driver tries the real 3-way merge FIRST, so non-overlapping edits on the
# two machines both survive; only where the sides genuinely collide does it keep
# the more recent one whole. [his, 2026-07-29] "which version of the board
# should we use should be determined by which one was the most recent."
#
# Requires merge.boardrecent.driver, which nix-docs-setup.sh registers on every
# run. Without that registration this line is INERT and git silently falls back
# to the default merge — i.e. back to the wedged sync. Verified end-to-end by
# tools/board-merge-test.sh.
board.md merge=boardrecent
